From 85c973028b785aa36ae592b08bbac76ab43c0593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grandgaev <rockbrock150@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:24:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: rule based split tunnelling router; fix first-packet
 loss with S4

router: new package that wraps the TUN device of a Device and applies
ordered routing rules (block/proxy/direct) made of Xray-style domain
matchers (full:/domain:/keyword:/regexp:) and IP prefixes. Domain rules
are applied by intercepting DNS (remote upstreams through the tunnel,
direct upstreams outside of it) and learning address->rule mappings from
the answers. Direct TCP is terminated in a gVisor netstack and
re-originated with sockets that bypass the tunnel; direct UDP and ICMP
echo are relayed at the packet level. Configured through new UAPI device
keys: routing_config_file, routing_bypass_ifindex[6], routing_bypass_ifname,
routing_bypass_fwmark. SetSocketProtector allows platforms such as
Android to protect the router's sockets.

device: the TUN reader cached the transport padding (S4) before blocking
in Read. As the device starts reading before it is configured, the first
packet sent after start-up carried no S4 prefix and was dropped by the
peer as a message of unknown type. Re-apply the current padding after
Read returns.

device: do not classify live transport packets as handshakes when
RandomTrailers relaxes the handshake size check (data loss with ranged
H1-H3 and different S values); fix a data race in timers; compare
endpoints by address when resetting the UDP window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
